course: dictionary
lesson: 9330
title: Spill: many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Spill is one of them, so the sentence around it tells you which meaning to use. «Mia spilled her juice on the table» means the juice fell out of the cup by accident.
explain: «Crowds spilled into the street» uses spill in another way. The crowd came pouring out over the edge of the building, like water running over the side of a full cup.
explain: «He spilled the beans» does not mean that beans are on the floor. It is an idiom, a set phrase, which means he told a secret. When a phrase makes no sense word by word, think about what the whole phrase means.
fact: Spill can be a verb, the action of letting something fall, or a noun, the mess itself: a spill.
fact: Spilled and spilt are both past forms of spill, so both are correct.
fact: «Spill the beans» means to tell a secret.
fact: Wipe up spills at once, because wet floors make people slip, and spilled hot drinks can burn.
fact: Oil spills harm birds and the sea, because oil does not mix with water and it coats birds' feathers.
exercise: «The waiter carried the tray carefully so nothing would spill.» What does spill mean here? | *Fall out of a container by accident | Ride a bike very fast | Count the cups | Shout loudly
exercise: «Crowds spilled into the street after the football match.» What does spilled mean here? | Stood still in a neat line | Was cleaned up | *Came pouring out over the edge of a place | Fell fast asleep
exercise: Jayden says «spill the beans» means beans fell on the floor. What does the phrase really mean? | *Tell a secret | Drop some food | Cook a big dinner | Count to ten
test: What is a spill? | *Liquid or stuff that has been spilled | A tiny insect that lives in water | A clean towel for drying hands | A loud shout
test: «Oil does not mix with water, so spilled oil spreads over the sea.» Why does spilled oil harm birds? | It stops the sea from moving | *It coats their feathers | Birds like the taste of oil | It makes the water warm
exam: In «the hot soup spilled on her arm», what does spilled mean? | Was eaten quickly | Was washed away by rain | Shouted at | *Fell out of the bowl by accident
